# Claude Adapter Rules

All Claude Code platform knowledge lives under `src/adapters/claude/`. Never add `.claude/` paths, frontmatter field names, or version checks to `src/core/`.

## Version matrix

- All version-sensitive behavior goes through `src/adapters/claude/version/matrix.ts`.
- Every non-trivial resolver rule needs a matrix entry and a fixture (SPEC §0.1 #3).
- Features without matrix entries resolve as `unknown`.

## Discovery (M0–M2)

- Read-only: never write to the scanned project's `.claude/**`.
- Only external process allowed in normal scan: `claude --version` (SPEC M0 #7).
- Register invalid agent files with specific reasons (A7).
- Mark same-directory name collisions as `ambiguous`; do not pick a winner (A4).

## Trust

- `blocked_by_trust` only for inline MCP in project agent frontmatter (R1) and project agent hooks (R5).
- Do not apply to `.mcp.json` servers or user-level agents (R4).

## Secrets

- Log and cache **key names** only — never env values, tokens, or MCP credentials (SPEC §0.1 #8).

## When uncertain

Return `unknown` with a reason. A confident wrong answer is worse than a missing feature.
